---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
const lessons = [
  ['01', 'Make your first skill reliable', 'Turn a recurring task into a skill. Compare a plain prompt with your skill, inspect a failure and check the next version on a fresh case.'],
  ['02', 'From a feature base to a working paywall', 'Prepare a reusable project base, fork a feature conversation and follow a test payment through to lesson access.'],
  ['03', 'Run tests when the agent stops', 'Write regression tests, watch them catch a broken access rule and use a Stop hook while building the lesson list.'],
  ['04', 'Let another agent prepare a lesson draft', 'Build one bounded operation, use it through a CLI and MCP, and check the draft it saves.'],
  ['05', 'Add a separate review pass', 'Give a fresh reviewer the request and the change. Verify its findings, make the fix and run the checks again.'],
  ['06', 'Shape a feature and build it with Kogen', 'Turn a request into acceptance examples and follow the work through shaping, approval, a build and verification.'],
  ['07', 'Keep one build session running', 'Queue prepared work, pick up later arrivals and recover after an interruption with a record of what happened.'],
];
---
<Site>
  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="headline">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="signal" aria-hidden="true"></span> Practical skills for working with coding agents</p>
        <h1 id="headline">Build your own<br />way of <span>working.</span></h1>
        <p class="intro">You already use coding agents. Learn to turn repeated instructions into skills, test what they do, and improve the workflow around them. Work with your own setup and build artifacts you can use again.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button plausible-event-name=Course+access+click" href="https://course.vibecodingforadults.com/">Get Season 1 · $49 <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a class="text-link" href="#course">Explore the curriculum <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
        </div>
        <p class="byline">With <a href="https://almirsarajcic.com">Almir Sarajčić</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-art" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="art-label">A way of working.<br />Made by you.</span>
        <img src="/brand/mark-light.svg" alt="" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high" />
        <span class="art-caption">Skills. Rules. Workflows.</span>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="method-band" aria-labelledby="method-title">
      <div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">From repeated instructions to reusable work</p><h2 id="method-title">Write it. Test it.<br /><span>Make it better.</span></h2></div>
      <ol class="method-grid wrap">
        <li><span class="number">01 / WRITE</span><h3>Make the task repeatable.</h3><p>Start with something you keep explaining to an agent. Write the instructions as a skill you can use again.</p></li>
        <li><span class="number">02 / TEST</span><h3>Check what comes out.</h3><p>Choose examples and observable checks. Keep the actual output so you can compare attempts.</p></li>
        <li><span class="number">03 / IMPROVE</span><h3>Change one thing.</h3><p>Learn from a failure, revise the skill and run it again. Try a case you have kept out of the revisions.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </section>
    <section class="course-section wrap" id="course" aria-labelledby="course-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Season one / Working curriculum</p><h2 id="course-title">Build the course.<br />Learn the workflow.</h2></div>
        <p>The running example is this course platform, built a piece at a time. Use the same methods on a project of your own.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="lesson-list">
        {lessons.map(([number, title, description]) => <li><span class="lesson-number">{number}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{description}</p></li>)}
      </ol>
      <p class="curriculum-note">Seven core lessons, with an optional eighth look behind the scenes at the course and platform. The lesson order and examples may evolve as the season is made.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="practice-section wrap" aria-labelledby="practice-title">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Watch. Try. Make your own.</p><h2 id="practice-title">The lesson continues<br />after the video.</h2><p>Each core lesson pairs a demonstration with explanatory notes, guided practice and a separate homework problem.</p></div>
      <dl class="format-list">
        <div><dt>10–15 minutes</dt><dd>A video with a real starting state, a demonstration and evidence of the result.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>10 minutes</dt><dd>Guided practice to try the method while the example is fresh.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>30 minutes</dt><dd>Homework on a different problem. Create your own skill, tool or workflow and keep the evidence.</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p class="format-note">These are target lengths. Agent generation and evaluation runs can take additional time.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="course-details wrap" aria-labelledby="details-title">
      <div class="details-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Bring your own setup</p><h2 id="details-title">Learn the method.<br />Use it in your work.</h2><p>The course uses coding agents, tests, scripts and tools such as Kogen as practical examples. You can follow the ideas with the tools you already use.</p><a class="text-link" href="/about/">About the course <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      <div class="price-card"><p class="eyebrow">Season one / Founding access</p><p class="price">$49 <span>USD / one payment</span></p><p>Keep access to the finished first season. The price for new buyers becomes $99 after the final lesson is released.</p><p class="price-note">Season one is taking shape. Videos are coming soon.</p><a class="button plausible-event-name=Course+access+click" href="https://course.vibecodingforadults.com/">Get Season 1 · $49 <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Site>
